# OpenTofu / Terraform.
#
# github/gitignore's Terraform template predates .tofu files, so this
# fragment carries the whole set rather than supplementing it.

# Provider and module downloads. Per root module, so the glob is not anchored.
.terraform/

# State. Only bootstrap keeps state locally; everything else is in S3. Committed
# state is both a merge conflict waiting to happen and a leak: it holds every
# attribute of every resource, including values a provider marked sensitive.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup

# Saved plans, written by `just tf-plan`. A plan file holds the variable values it
# was built with in cleartext.
*.tfplan

# Crash logs, which contain the full request and response bodies.
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Variable files holding real values. envs/*.tfvars IS committed -- it carries
# per-environment configuration, never a secret -- so it is excluded from this rule.
*.auto.tfvars
terraform.tfvars
!infra/envs/*.tfvars

# Override files: local-only customisation by design.
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# CLI configuration, which can hold credentials and mirror settings.
.terraformrc
terraform.rc

# The lock file is COMMITTED and deliberately absent from this list. It is what
# pins provider versions and hashes across the team and CI; `just tf-lock`
# regenerates it for every platform.
